{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1003857-apocalypse-scenarios","id":1003857,"title":"Apocalypse Scenarios","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-16T04:20:14-08:00","id":1003857,"title":"Apocalypse Scenarios","content":"What would you think would be a good apocalypse scenarios for CoD? (Assume nobody can/will stop it in tracks).<br /> <br /> One good idea is a spirit invasion. The idea is given in the Werewolf book and there is also a mention in the description of one of Mage legacies that spirit nobility is aggitated with recent human actions. Human civilization as a whole has no means to fight off organised attack from the shadow. <br /> The other is a scenario from WoD werewolf. What is someone (Thyrsus, Forces master, werewolf) detonate Yellowstone. The result would simply devastate the world through Ice age and starvation. Jnaknamunti sound like good perpetrators. <br /> Then of course are more esoteric means, like madness viruses, mass zombie raising, self-summoning uber demons and many other. What do you think, what would be thematically appropriate and interesting Apocalypse scenario for CoD?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T06:47:55-08:00","id":1003907,"title":"","content":"Here is a thread for <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/982175-gameline-as-zombie-apocalypse\">Zombie Apocalypse</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T06:54:20-08:00","id":1003911,"title":"","content":"I think there was another thread like this, but I can't remember the title.<br /> <br /> How flexible are we talking with Apocalypse here? Would a mass vanishing (Rapture) event count? Maybe Mages partially Ascended part of the population (or just ended up dumping them elsewhere). How about a temporal reversal? Maybe malfunctioning Infrastructure sends the geographical area of West Virginia or Great Britain into the past (hundreds or even thousands of years). What about single, but far reaching adjustments to the status quo? Like a human messes up the Contract of Electricity, costing humanity the applied use of electricity (no power or electronics).<br /> <br /> <sub>Bonus points to whoever catches the references.</sub>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-16-2016, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T11:08:08-08:00","id":1004014,"title":"","content":"GMC got a few apocalyptic scenarios.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T11:23:07-08:00","id":1004023,"title":"","content":"World of Darkness: Mirrors also has a couple of apocalyse situations, though it more addresses how players would handle it than how it would happen. I believe one was an alien invasion. There were also merits that players could take in such situations, such as protective equipment or water filtration metods, or even just shelter.<br /> <br /> Edit: my apologies, what I remembered as merits were just rolls players could make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 11-16-2016, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T11:39:31-08:00","id":1004030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1003857-apocalypse-scenarios?p=1003911#post1003911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there was another thread like this, but I can't remember the title.</div> </div> </div> </div>perhaps <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17747-1001-apoclypses-or-a-collection-of-tier-4-story-hooks\">this</a> one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T18:03:20-08:00","id":1004183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1003857-apocalypse-scenarios?p=1003911#post1003911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there was another thread like this, but I can't remember the title.<br /> <br /> How flexible are we talking with Apocalypse here? Would a mass vanishing (Rapture) event count? Maybe Mages partially Ascended part of the population (or just ended up dumping them elsewhere). How about a temporal reversal? Maybe malfunctioning Infrastructure sends the geographical area of West Virginia or Great Britain into the past (hundreds or even thousands of years). What about single, but far reaching adjustments to the status quo? Like a human messes up the Contract of Electricity, costing humanity the applied use of electricity (no power or electronics).<br /> <br /> <sub>Bonus points to whoever catches the references.</sub></div> </div> </div> </div>That's a Revolution reference, isn't it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T18:21:35-08:00","id":1004191,"title":"","content":"There's a few of them in the God Machine Chronicle book, and I believe War Against the Pure and a few other werewolf books mention them, as does Mirrors.<br /> <br /> In vampire there's the edimmu, who are potentially a vampire-ending threat with their habit of taking over vampires, compelling diablerie and multiplying rapidly.<br /> <br /> Werewolf has the hosts and idigam, any of which can become an apocalyptic situation. At least some of the Pure are trying to bring back Pangaea, and would love the opportunity to either start an earthly apocalypse or create a situation that would have the same results. If the Gauntlet falls, spirits will steamroll over humanity in a very nasty way.<br /> <br /> Mage has some weirdnesses similar to those of werewolf. Most, but not all, are connected to the Abyss.<br /> <br /> Mirrors has the more 'standard' apocalypses. The Masquerade falling, nuclear armageddon, zombie apocalypse, alien invasion, asteroid impact, the aforementioned spiritual incursion. The Mirrors book didn't offer that much in the way of fluff but it did give some neat mechanical systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T22:12:55-08:00","id":1004250,"title":"","content":"thanks everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}